KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp26
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ saturated: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Saturation arithmetic ([numeric.sat]) with N5008's names add_sat and
saturate_cast.  libstdc++ 16 implements it as saturating_add and
saturating_cast, names from a revision after N5008.  No standard library
implements it yet (libstdc++ 16, libc++ 18), so the test is written to N5008
and not checked with a compiler; it is FUTURE until a library provides the
header.  Then it is a KNOWNBUG or CORE test of CBMC's support of that library
code.
